---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Contact from '../components/Contact.astro';
import { site } from '../site';
---

<Base title="About" description="Ken Nichol: senior full-stack engineer on Vancouver Island, building for the web since 2004.">
  <section>
    <div class="wrap split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
        <h1>Ken Nichol</h1>
        <p class="muted">{site.role}<br />{site.location}</p>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p class="lede" style="max-width: none">
          I'm the engineer teams bring in when a web platform still matters but has become slow, risky or expensive to
          change.
        </p>
        <h2>Background</h2>
        <p>
          I started doing professional web work in 2004 at North Island Studios, and went independent as Nichol Web
          Consulting in 2008. Most of those years were spent deep in PHP and WordPress: custom themes and plugins,
          integrations, migrations and long-term care of sites that businesses ran on.
        </p>
        <p>
          I joined Toptal in 2019 as a WordPress developer and later added its full-stack specialization. My recent
          engagements have been modernization work: moving an enterprise platform to headless Next.js and Payload CMS,
          upgrading theme frameworks across major versions, and building the CI/CD pipelines that make deployments
          boring.
        </p>
        <p>
          I'm also a Star Mentor at Zero To Mastery, where I help developers learning to code build solid
          foundations. Explaining things clearly is a large part of the job, with juniors and with executives.
        </p>

        <h2>How I work</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>I treat the existing system as the spec.</strong> Before replacing anything, I find out what it actually
            does, including what nobody wrote down.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>I'm straight about scope.</strong> If something is outside what I've done before, I'll say so before we
            start, not after.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>I document as I go.</strong> Runbooks and decision notes are part of the deliverable, so your team isn't
            dependent on me.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>I use AI tools with review.</strong> Claude Code and Cursor make me faster; they don't decide what ships.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Elsewhere</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><a href={site.links.toptal}>Toptal profile</a></li>
          <li><a href={site.links.linkedin}>LinkedIn</a></li>
          <li><a href={site.links.github}>GitHub</a>, including <a href="https://github.com/kennithnichol/nicholweb.ca">the source for this site</a></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <Contact />
</Base>
